		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42486</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/perplexity.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" /></p>
<p>        Perplexity is launching "Teammates," always-on agents that work through ongoing projects on their own virtual machines. The feature requires the Max plan at $200 per month, well above similar offerings from OpenAI or Anthropic. The market for always-on agents is getting crowded.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/perplexity-now-has-its-own-always-on-ai-agent/">Perplexity now has its own always-on AI agent</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
